{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>One lot for HaShem and one lot for Azazel.</b> It appears that these two goats are exactly like the two kids of the goats that Jacob prepared for Isaac — and he made one of them seasoned (מַטְעַמִּים) according to the palate's liking, and this is the portion of Samael, who was given a bribe so that Jacob would receive the blessings through his portion, from the side of the second kid, which he prepared as a Pesach-offering to HaShem, as is found in the Midrash (Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 32) — for it was on that day, the first day of Pesach. Isaac said: My son, the treasure-houses of dew are opened today, etc. So too for all generations: by means of these two goats, Samael is given his portion, so that Jacob may receive his portion from the lot that is for HaShem. And so the Midrash (Bereshit Rabbah 65:14) expounds the verse that says 'good kids of goats' — good for you, for through them you will receive the blessings; and good for your children, for through them atonement is made on Yom Kippur."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The word חומר ('matter' / 'palate') is ambiguous; I rendered it as 'the palate's liking' following the reading מַטְעַמִּים as seasoned food, though the text could alternatively mean 'as the matter required.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:36:57.822561712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}